{
  "Rashi on Eruvin 15a:1:1": {
    "hebrew": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">העומד מאליו</strong> - שלא הוקבע שם לשם תיקון מבוי, דלא הזמינוהו לכך:",
    "english": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">That stands by itself</strong> - That it was not established there for the purpose of rectifying the alleyway, as they did not designate it for this [purpose].",
    "status": "pending"
  },
  "Rashi on Eruvin 15a:2:1": {
    "english": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">Where we did not rely on it from yesterday</strong> - For there was another side post there, and it fell on Shabbat.",
    "status": "pending"
  },
  "Rashi on Eruvin 15a:4:1": {
    "english": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">To make use of the tree</strong> - And he will climb up and detach [fruit or branches] on Yom Tov.",
    "status": "pending"
  },
  "Rashi on Eruvin 15a:5:1": {
    "english": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">[If] there was there</strong> - [This baraita] is taught in the second chapter regarding <i>passei bira’ot</i> [posts around cisterns].",
    "status": "pending"
  },
  "Rashi on Eruvin 15a:5:2": {
    "hebrew": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">חיצת הקנים</strong> - קנים מחוברים. חיצת — שהיו נטועים כסדר מחיצה:",
    "english": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">A partition of reeds</strong> - Reeds attached [to the ground]. [The word] <i>chitzat</i> [means] that they were planted in the arrangement of a partition.",
    "status": "pending"
  },
  "Rashi on Eruvin 15a:5:3": {
    "hebrew": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">דיומד</strong> - מפרש בפ' שני: דיו עמודין — עמוד אחד נראה כשנים, שעשאו כמרזב, ונוטה אחד ממחיצותיו לדרום ואחד למערב, דכי עביד ד' דיומדין לד' הפיאות, יש לכל מחיצה ב' אמות עומד — אמה מכאן ואמה מכאן: <span class=\"image-ref-container\"><span class=\"image-ref-text\">(*):</span><span class=\"image-ref\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></span></span><span class=\"image-pointer\">(*)</span>",
    "english": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">A double post [<i>dyomad</i>]</strong> - [The Gemara] explains in the second chapter: [It is a contraction of] <i>dyo amudin</i> [two posts] — a single post that appears like two, which he made like a gutter, and one of its walls extends to the south and one to the west; so that when he makes four double posts for the four corners, each partition has two cubits of standing [wall] — a cubit from this [side] and a cubit from that [side]. <span class=\"image-ref-container\"><span class=\"image-ref-text\">(*):</span><span class=\"image-ref\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></span></span><span class=\"image-pointer\">(*)</span>",
    "status": "pending"
  },
  "Tosafot on Eruvin 15a:4:1": {
    "hebrew": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">תא שמע העושה סוכתו</strong> - בפ' הישן <span class=\"parenthesized\">(סוכה דף כד:)</span> מוקי לה דעביד לה בהוצא ודפנא, דלא תקשי לרב אחא בר יעקב, דאמר: \"כל מחיצה שאינה יכולה לעמוד ברוח\" — פירוש: שהרוח מנענעת' לכאן ולכאן — \"אינה מחיצה\"; ואמאי כשרה? והא קאזיל ואתי! ולפי זה לא פריך הכא מידי, והוה מצי למימר: \"ולטעמיך\". אי נמי, משמע ליה דמיירי בכל ענין: בין הוי רוב דופן מעובי האילן שאינו הולך ברוח, בין דהוי רוב דופן מן הנוף:",
    "english": "<strong class=\"dibur-hamatchil\">\"Come and hear: One who makes his <i>sukkah</i>\"</strong> - In chapter HaYashen (Sukkah 24b), [the Gemara] establishes [the Mishnah as referring to a case] where he made it with palm branches and bay leaves, so that it will not pose a difficulty for Rav Aḥa bar Ya'akov, who said: \"Any partition that cannot stand in the wind\" — meaning that the wind sways it back and forth — \"is not a partition\"; and [otherwise,] why is it valid? Behold, it sways back and forth! And according to this, [the Gemara] poses no difficulty here, and it could have said: \"And according to your reasoning!\" Alternatively, [the Gemara here] understood that [the Mishnah] speaks of every case: whether the majority of the wall is from the thickness of the tree [trunk], which does not sway in the wind, or whether the majority of the wall is from the foliage.",
    "status": "pending"
  }
}
